  "subtitle": "The arcade game you played with an actual beer tap",
  "why_scout_cares": "Tapper is the definitive example of a real-world physical prop repurposed as a computer game controller. Early cabinets used actual Budweiser beer tap handles — not a replica, not a metaphor, but the same tap handle you'd find in a bar. The cabinet was designed as bar furniture with a brass foot rail and drink holders. No other exhibit in the museum turns a found object from everyday life into the primary game interface. The interaction model — pull to pour, release to slide — maps a natural physical affordance directly to on-screen action.",
  "search_terms": ["tapper arcade 1984", "beer tap controller", "bally midway root beer tapper", "marvin glass and associates"],
